    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-351016",
      "knowledge_point_id": "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759",
      "knowledge_point": "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}{log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}{log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}{log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}{log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}-{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(8x)\\,(x){|}_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}-{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}x(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{log}_{3}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3}}{8})\\,(\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8})-{log}_{3}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{1}{8})\\,(\\frac{1}{8})]-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{\\int }_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8}{log}_{3}⁡({e}^{3})-\\frac{1}{8}{log}_{3}⁡(1)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}x{|}_{1/8}^{{e}^{3}/8} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}(\\frac{{e}^{3}}{8}-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}(2{e}^{3}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
